<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="2">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Fade in:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FLASHY NEWS PACKAGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Images of chemical dumps, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">hazmat</Text>
      <Text> suits, crying orphans. Dramatic music plays over the top.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly Mae (v.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And it may already be too late...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>Fade out:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DANE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KELLY MAE"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. News Desk</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Fascinating story, Kelly Mae.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And to think, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">I</Text>
      <Text> use that same brand of mouth wash.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae nods and Dane addresses the camera:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well for everyone here at the NoHo Rag. I’m Dane Argyle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly Mae</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And I’m Kelly Mae Greenblatt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Y’all have yourselves a good night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>MUSIC STINGER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>TITLE CARD</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>Cut to:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BOB"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. News Desk - Behind camera</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob takes his signature sigh of relief. Then holds his stomach in disbelief.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh wow...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A hand juts into frame with a bottle of Pepto.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob waves it off as he looks around to the crew in the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I don’t think I need Pepto after this episode!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Great work Kelly Mae!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And Dane! Not a single reference to your digestive system!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Progress!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>This is what progress looks like, people!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob attempts to lead the crew on a round of applause but no one joins in and he quickly feels awkward and just as quickly rebounds into enthusiasm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob points around the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Game night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Game night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob’s question piques Dane’s interest.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>Cut to:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DANE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KELLY MAE"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. News Desk</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane and Kelly Mae remain sitting at the news desk but more casually.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Game night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly Mae</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You didn’t get the email?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Bob invited us to his home tonight for the semi-annual employee game night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He said to expect booze, board games and bonding!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane’s eyebrow raises.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Which board game?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KELLY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The game of LIFE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Ooh</Text>
      <Text>! I’m in!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’ve been crushing that game since birth!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>Cut to:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 6/8" Page="3" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BOB"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DANE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KELLY MAE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="OLIVIA"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. Bob’s apartment - about three hours later</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob’s apartment is neat but lived in, basically Chaz’ place since that’s where we’re shooting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The four members of the main staff are sitting around the kitchen table. In this order: Dane, Kelly Mae, Olivia then Bob.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The group is playing the board game LIFE. Empty beers line the table next to the recycle bin. Everyone has clearly had at least two drinks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Why isn’t </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">news anchor</Text>
      <Text> an available profession in this game?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly Mae</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Did you just find the next Dane Expose?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob becomes interested in the exchange.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hey yeah, We still need to have a postmortem about that Santa story.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I think you are the only person in the world that thought those cookies looked like hairy vaginas.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And poor Santa.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Now everyone in NoHo hates him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Olivia’s interest is piqued.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Olivia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Good.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Our corporate owners have made Santa a strange omniscient morality judge for centuries.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae spins the move spinner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Olivia (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s about time Santa gets taken down a peg.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae moves her game piece as Olivia finishes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well, take that peg and give it to Kelly Mae!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>She’s having another baby!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae collapses into her seat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KellY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Can I just...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Not...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Have that baby?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob scoffs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That’s not in the rules, Kelly Mae.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KELLY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah, but can’t we...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Like...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Be progressive about this?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I apologize for the traditional values of the board game LIFE, Kelly Mae, but the rules say you get a beautiful baby girl!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>As Bob speaks he reaches into the bag of babies, pulls out a pink one, stretches across the table and sticks the baby in Kelly Mae’s game piece.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KELLY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Greaaaaaaat</Text>
      <Text>...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane sips his beer while he scrutinizes Olivia. Olivia feels his gaze and stares back awkwardly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m sure I’ve asked you this before.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But who are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae slaps Dane.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Olivia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m Olivia!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m the writer here!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane stares at Olivia like she’s lying then turns to Bob.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We have a writer for this show?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Everyone else at the table nods.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Huh, I guess I never thought a news show </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">used</Text>
      <Text> one!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Where do you think the words in the Teleprompter come from?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane shrugs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I don’t know...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The newspaper?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae addresses Bob and Olivia while looking at Dane. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly Mae</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>There it is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Olivia takes it in stride.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Olivia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’ve worked here for nearly two years. I write everything you read.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You’re welcome.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane straightens his back as a beaming smile crests his face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>No no, you’re welcome.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane spins the move spinner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Annnnnd</Text>
      <Text>... We’ve now reached Full Dane.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to Bob, Olivia)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m very sorry you guys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane looks down at the board and shifts his piece a few spaces.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">And</Text>
      <Text>, I landed on a house!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to Kelly Mae)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Add that beautiful split level ranch to my portfolio, my dear!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae stares blankly at Dane.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Kelly MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh, so I’m your assistant now?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Good point.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to Bob)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>So when do we get assistants?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob bristles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>We’ve just gotten the show out of a ratings nose dive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m just happy we’re still on the air.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Do your part, build the viewership, and maybe in a year or two we can talk about assistants.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Ratings nose dive?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You mean, Reidel?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob bristles again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...Let me get the Pepto.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">Crossfade</Text>
      <Text> to:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ALEC"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BOB"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. Bob’s Office - Jake’s place</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec sits at the desk, leaning back with his legs up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He tosses the MAGIC 8 BALL from hand to hand, not bothering to look at the message that would surface.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob (v.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Alec was able to effortlessly push me to the brink of insanity.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I guess his intense drive to tell the news made him blind to my suffering.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob enters.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Is that little Alec?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec drops his feet from the desk and sits upright.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Alec</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Bob, it’s Mister Reidel now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob stops in his tracks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh, I’m...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sorry...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Mister-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec bursts out laughing and stands to slap Bob on the shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m just messing with you!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Call me Alec.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob laughs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Okay, Alec. I just wanted to go over the show format with you once more.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Bob, Bob, Bob. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You forget, I’m a Reidel.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Telling the news is in my blood. We’ll be just fine!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec grabs hold of Bob’s shoulder as he speaks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Alec (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Look, I’ve just inherited this show from my dad.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s mine now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And, I want you to work as hard for me as you did when my dad was in charge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec exits briskly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob turns and watches Alec go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BOB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Your dad worked for </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">me</Text>
      <Text>...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>Cut to:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="8" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BOB"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DANE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KELLY MAE"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="OLIVIA"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. Game Night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane and Kelly Mae sit enraptured in the story.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That was nearly two years ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>His first day.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And the first time I saw him since he was a kid.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Olivia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He was...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Forceful. But virtuous.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I just wish Alec didn’t reject all my stories.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to Bob)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And I wish you fought more for me!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob looks sheepish.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well, I...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Look...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s just...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Uhh</Text>
      <Text>... Who’s turn is it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae spins and moves her game piece.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KELLY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Another baby?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>These </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="Bold">are</Text>
      <Text> your child bearing years, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">KM</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Bob, Kelly Mae is going to need a second car for all of her babies!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(pointing to himself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And this guy right here needs a potty break!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane gets up and walks off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bob leans in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>So, this is Dane Argyle, is it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Kelly Mae waves Bob off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>KellY MAE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah... He’s an acquired taste, but he’s a good guy to have in your corner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He’s a little rough around the edges, and he’ll drive you crazy, but he loves telling the news, even if he doesn’t quite understand how it’s made.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dane returns to the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Dane</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Candies in the bathroom?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Producer Bob, you fancy!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bob</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Those aren’t candies!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>They are decorative soaps!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DANE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well, they were delicious.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Olivia laughs, which makes Bob then Kelly Mae laugh, it grows to uproarious levels.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Fade to black</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

